  "The B text, in The National Archives at Kew, was written at the end of the thirteenth century, probably at the Cistercian abbey of Neath, and runs to 1286. The C text, in the British Library’s Cotton collection, was written at St Davids and runs to 1288. Both carry the story on through the age of the princes, and they are the roots from which grew the Welsh chronicles, the Brutiau.",
